x86_64-linux  `_ZN1TC1Ei` and `_ZN1TD1Ev`, and nothing else. clang emits only the base-object C2 and D2 forms of a constructor and destructor defined inside their class on this target and calls those directly, where cxx1 emits the complete-object forms beside them - identical bodies for a class with no virtual base, mergeable definitions both, so the cost is object size and nothing else. The same fact move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames already record, and it is why this file has no x86_64-windows or arm64-darwin line: both of those agree with clang name for name.
